# The script `mise run ffi-test` hands the headless mode of an editor built
# from the core alone (the set `tests/empty-set`, which is the default set
# with its packages dropped), with the config in `config/`, which is empty.
# No package of that set supplies an input scheme: the Vim scheme is the
# default package `evil`'s (packages/evil/). So the editor refuses to
# start: it prints the one line of `expected` on stderr and exits 1, before
# it reads this script or loads the config, and runs no directive below.
# `editor --probe`, which a restart runs before it hands the session over,
# is refused with the same line and status. It touches no file.

reload
settle
scene
